From c28b6586f74f7fb37c071174b66a445cf4ce0884 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Ding <yi.s.ding@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 30 Jul 2026 13:58:48 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] media: rkvdec: do not destroy the SRAM provider pool

of_gen_pool_get() returns a pool owned by the SRAM provider; it does
not transfer ownership to the consumer. If V4L2 initialization fails
after RKVDEC obtains that pool, the probe error path destroys the
provider-owned object and can leave the provider or another consumer
with stale state.

Drop only the consumer's use of the borrowed pointer and leave pool
destruction to its owner.

Fixes: e5640dbb991c ("media: rkvdec: Add RCB and SRAM support")
Signed-off-by: Yi Ding <yi.s.ding@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkvdec/rkvdec.c | 3 ---
 1 file changed, 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkvdec/rkvdec.c b/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkvdec/rkvdec.c
index 3f90228b66561..cc1dbbcb00b41 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkvdec/rkvdec.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkvdec/rkvdec.c
@@ -1948,9 +1948,6 @@ static int rkvdec_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	pm_runtime_dont_use_autosuspend(&pdev->dev);
 	pm_runtime_disable(&pdev->dev);
 
-	if (rkvdec->sram_pool)
-		gen_pool_destroy(rkvdec->sram_pool);
-
 	return ret;
 }
 
